{"type":"text","timestamp":1791649289988,"sessionID":"ses_a9db22424ca80a3ad43b","part":{"id":"prt_1269e8b370012Q9VGLcAsqaXn9","sessionID":"ses_a9db22424ca80a3ad43b","messageID":"msg_1269e8333001zu0wwUaIhLN0b4","type":"text","text":"**Defect — `parser.py:2`:** `bool(value)` checks truthiness, not valid Boolean strings. Consequently:\n- `\"false\"` incorrectly returns `True`.\n- `\"invalid\"` returns `True` and `\"\"` returns `False`, instead of raising `ValueError`.\n\n**Recommendation:** Explicitly accept only `\"true\"` → `True` and `\"false\"` → `False`; raise `ValueError` for everything else. Do not normalize case or whitespace.\n\nPrevent recurrence with regression tests covering both valid strings and rejected inputs: unknown strings, empty strings, uppercase variants, surrounding whitespace, and non-string values.\n\nNo files changed.","time":{"start":1791649286967,"end":1791649289988}}}
